 Basic Excel Integration Questions
	1. Can Selenium interact with Excel files directly?
		○ No, Selenium itself does not support Excel handling. You need external libraries like Apache POI .
	2. Which library is commonly used to read/write Excel files in Java?
		○ Apache POI (org.apache.poi package)
	3. What is the difference between .xls and .xlsx in Apache POI?
		○ .xls (Excel 97–2003): Use HSSFWorkbook
		○ .xlsx (Excel 2007+): Use XSSFWorkbook
		
Common Code-Based Questions
	1. How do you read data from an Excel cell using Apache POI?
FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream("data.xlsx");
XSSFWorkbook workbook = new XSSFWorkbook(fis);
XSSFSheet sheet = workbook.getSheet("Sheet1");
String value = sheet.getRow(0).getCell(0).getStringCellValue();
System.out.println(value);
workbook.close();
	2. How do you write data to an Excel file using Java?
FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream("data.xlsx");
XSSFWorkbook workbook = new XSSFWorkbook(fis);
XSSFSheet sheet = workbook.getSheet("Sheet1");
sheet.getRow(0).createCell(1).setCellValue("Passed");
FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream("data.xlsx");
workbook.write(fos);
workbook.close();
fos.close();
	3. How do you get the number of rows in an Excel sheet?
int rowCount = sheet.getLastRowNum();  // 0-based index
	4. How do you handle different Excel cell types (string, numeric, boolean)?
Cell cell = sheet.getRow(0).getCell(0);
switch (cell.getCellType()) {
    case STRING: System.out.println(cell.getStringCellValue()); break;
    case NUMERIC: System.out.println(cell.getNumericCellValue()); break;
    case BOOLEAN: System.out.println(cell.getBooleanCellValue()); break;
}
